work-graph.json:354:      "remaining": "Bounded core/state/effects/resource/navigation values and strict UI codecs are tested; full lifecycle/restoration, platform parity and broader public adoption remain open. FieldLog now uses the public state/effect API for its native task editor; full MixerUI/guest adoption is still pending. Guest UI checkpoint: bounded SDK42 Debug/Release and19 TSan tests, packaged bridge48 per host mode, signed activation113 per mode, independent repaired-race review, public privacy checks and complete iOS/Android module compilation now pass. Native Apple model12 Debug/Release and11 TSan tests pass; the subsequently completed signed Mac native window flow now verifies click, stored bytes, display health and joined close. Android signed presentation, full Swift execution/size, published consumer and physical/GA gates remain open. Hosted35a9a36 passed GCC fixture/bridge48 per mode/activation113, then found SwiftUI teardown reentrant publication. Scoped repair passes13 presentation tests per Debug/Release plus12 TSan,2 independent probes and mobile module compilation; pinned hosted/current-repair native visible qualification remain pending. Pinned teardown CI5a5b395 and fresh current-source Mac native save/health/storage/close flow now pass; caaa005 remains a failed CI run; independent noise reproduces unsound observer accounting, repaired test-only observers preserve exact assertions and measurements in Debug/Release with and without noise. The exact CI allocation origin is unattributed. Hosted92e93b2 and e299f1a now pass all three jobs. Private Android host binding and fresh-source CI runner now have scoped root/independent acceptance: 39 ordinary cases per Debug/Release/TSan, nine independent lifecycle replays, 15 CI checks per normal/optimized Python, and 4,149 root acceptance bindings. S4-21 actual JNI stale delivery, S4-29 optimized Release lifetime-counter injection and hosted pinned Swift 6.2.4 new-runner execution remain pending. No native Android authority, signed core integration, physical/published FieldLog/release/GA pass. Separate JNI/Java contract design is next. Updated product-plan section8.3 requires shared-theme design parity: same layout, hierarchy, content, colors, typography scale, iconography, spacing and component appearance on iOS/Android. Current platform-default controls do not satisfy it. Shared appearance schema and both adapters require coordinated implementation, explicit opt-in for platform-specific app appearance, and side-by-side physical reference-screen review. Native accessibility/navigation/text input and system-owned surfaces remain native. Legitimate text-shaping/rasterization/density/safe-area differences are permitted. Physical design-parity evidence remains pending while phones are disconnected; prior interaction receipts do not qualify this requirement. Hosted61c5c8b Swift6.2.4 now passes fresh Android host Debug/Release/TSan with39ordinary cases each; root verifies579Git-input/log hashes and the downloaded artifact digest. Services passes; overall run fails minimal-feature GlobalView dead-code Clippy after tests pass. Descriptor-only fix atd6c41a0 passes202minimal tests perD/R and4Clippy combinations locally; d6c41a0 hostedVM/Swift/services all pass, including the fresh Swift6.2.4 Android host runner. No native JNI, S4-21, S4-29 Release injection, physical design parity or GA acceptance inferred. JNI/Java stage5 design is root accepted after11declaration/audit commands and81exact bindings; all50native/visual/external implementation cases remain pending. Shared appearance foundation, closed native Swift backend, Java subset, actual JNI/Looper/window observation and signed-core composition remain required; no native or GA authority follows from declarations. Data-only SDK packet encoder and shared pending-frontier repair accepted after158root bindings,51SDKtests perDebug/Release,16productionJava decoder assertions,3public return events, officialiOS/Android modules