work-graph.json:4528:      "remaining": "Shared defined/indirect call and fetch/run orchestration is integrated with scoped host acceptance. Complete initializer/Ready/private fixed-target lifecycle, then separately reviewed public invocation. Preserve accepted private numeric/value/frame/control/memory/bulk/growth/imported-host mechanics and fail-closed bounds. Complete supported-profile conformance/differential/fuzz/resource-limit qualification, source diagnostics, performance/memory/size, native joins, immutable published FieldLog consumption and D3/GA acceptance.",
work-graph.json:4529:      "currentCheckpoint": "Underlying fixture-only envelope source and bounded accounting have scoped independent host acceptance: 78 producer methods, 14 exact-source independent methods plus 2 separate test-overlay methods, API1+8, 21,714 fresh candidate comparisons and 32 layouts; root verified 407 source/accounting/review members. No semantic replay, live VM/CLI/target or GA acceptance. Portable CI runner round1 was rejected for ambiguous compiler identity and unrelated diagnostic spans. Corrected runner passes 32 normal/optimized controls and one fresh full Rust1.99 host closure; independent correction review now passes and root accepts the scoped runner. Exact CI wiring is applied; delivery and actual Rust1.98.1 CI remain pending. The earlier complete target still fails Corpus1 CacheWork; no optimization has been accepted from this fixture work.",
work-graph.json:4530:      "nextImplementation": "Implement the selected standalone fixture cache-state Rust closure within unchanged source/work/move/caller/lifetime/cleanup bounds, then freeze source and proofs for independent actual-File review. Existing APIs/ABI/report and the immutable envelope pack remain fixed; live VM/target/native work remains unselected.",
work-graph.json:4531:      "lifecycleCheckpoint": "The private Swift lifecycle V3 candidate now has root acceptance for its selected host matrix: all 30 rows pass, comprising 1,602 test executions and four compile checks. The four focused contexts pass 23 lifecycle tests each; Swift and all-feature libraries, Frozen regressions and both qualified Node oracle runs also pass. Root verifies all 978 sealed files and all 30 target cleanups. V2\u2019s failed ticket assertion remains preserved; V3 changes its expectation to match retained decoded-cache ownership without changing engine limits. The exact three-file private implementation is now integrated: the full 132-file VM source closure matches the tested candidate, and 23 focused live tests plus Swift-only Clippy pass. Its fresh target is removed. The complete SL matrix, guest table mutation, real full reactor, native execution, FieldLog and GA remain pending.",
work-graph.json:4534:      "exactReactorDiagnosticCheckpoint": "The exact 53,777,114-byte full Swift FieldLog reactor passes owned validation of 79,832 bodies and 6,505,659 instructions, adoption and runtime construction. Initialization stops at a test-only 64-entry release observer assertion; neither corpus call runs. Root verifies 246 sealed files plus three external bindings. The original failure is preserved, the process group is empty and owned scratch is removed. A narrow test-only observer repair is underway; full-reactor execution, native/public/signed use and GA remain pending. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-diagnostic.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
work-graph.json:4536:      "exactReactorAfterObserverCheckpoint": "The full Swift FieldLog reactor now passes complete owned validation and real initialization. Its first corpus stops at the unchanged CacheWork limit: attempted 64,000,001 of 64,000,000, after 24,054 decodes and 23,990 evictions; the second corpus is unrun. Original consuming cleanup returns primary reservations, tickets and live counters to zero while retaining the failure. Root verifies 214 sealed members and four external bindings; owned scratch is removed. Cache-work optimization analysis is underway without widening bounds. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
work-graph.json:4537:      "cacheResetElisionSelection": "Root selects a narrow private Swift cache candidate after source-bound diagnosis: two redundant 512-slot clearing loops account for at least 24,631,296 credits in the failed target run. A finite actual-cache fixture confirms the cost; this is not measured target CPU attribution or a completion prediction. The additive contract removes only those operations, retaining initialized scratch, explicit pass-boundary checks and all original limits. Implementation and acceptance are pending; no new full-reactor attempt is selected. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-contract.md and verification/swift-cache-reset-elision-root-selection/selection.json.",
work-graph.json:4538:      "cacheResetElisionCheckpoint": "Root accepts and integrates the private Swift cache reset elimination: two redundant 512-slot writes are removed, retaining initialized scratch and pass-boundary checks under unchanged limits. The producer matrix passes default/compatibility/all-feature Debug and Release with existing ignores retained; six fresh root live tests pass at VM closure b28da766c84b6353a4511e2fc3fbcb0d4302d5b8a5a74da1ee3d7fb776ca2c11. Owned build targets are removed. A separate unchanged full-reactor attempt is being prepared; no target, native, signed, published FieldLog or GA pass is claimed. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-checkpoint.md.",
work-graph.json:4542:      "residentIndexCandidateCheckpoint": "The isolated private Swift resident index passes 626 all-feature Release tests with nine inherited ignores, 29 cache Debug tests, default/compatibility suites, Clippy and scoped formatting. Root verifies all 570 sealed members and the unchanged live VM closure. The finite 256-hit fixture uses 2,048 versus 8,832 credits; fixed cache accounting increases by 840 bytes and foundation accounting by 384 bytes under unchanged limits. Independent review is underway; no live integration or full-reactor retry is selected. See docs/swift-cache-resident-index.md.",
