work-graph.json:13350:      "customerAuthorizationPostgres": "Root accepts the finite durable PostgreSQL lookup and selected fixture/migration integration after verifying 656 retained bindings and 25 current inputs. Final independent CI-fixture and standalone modes each pass the same 25 product methods plus 17 independent probes; all five migrations apply/idempotently rerun and the latest two roll back/reapply. Predefined pg_ role membership now rejects directly and indirectly. Original failed role, rollback and collector-preservation attempts remain intact. Runtime is read-only; scoped FORCE RLS and six canonical revocation locks supply evidence to the existing pure policy. Default adapter remains unavailable. Full standard CI/PostgreSQL 16, actual existing build-worker assertions, trusted-clock before-effect checks, domain/audit/idempotency/Oban transactions, customer HTTP/console and deployed topology/GA remain pending. See docs/hosted-customer-authorization-postgres-review.md and verification/hosted-customer-authorization-postgres-root-acceptance/acceptance.json.",
