work-graph.json:14105:      "latestHostedCI": "Checkpoint `5906779f` passes all three Engine CI jobs and all 38 steps without skips. The later `2fc068b8` checkpoint is pushed; its services and VM jobs pass while Swift remains running at this observation. See verification/github-ci-5906779f-engine/receipt.json and verification/github-delivery-2fc068b8/. These are host checks, not operational or GA acceptance.",
work-graph.json:14106:      "buildAdmissionCheckpoint": "The hosted build coordinator now has durable capacity limits per organization/platform, retained worker reservations and expiring owner/epoch leases. PostgreSQL row locks serialize admission; expiry never frees a possibly running worker, stale coordinators cannot mutate it, and release requires matching terminal evidence. Root and independent review accept 227 host tests, including 17 admission tests and 11 independent controls. The corrected UTC fixture proves expiry crosses during a real lock wait; two existing Linux-only identity tests remain skipped on this Mac. All 86 collected source inputs and 19 command logs verify, production test consumers are absent, and disposable PostgreSQL cleanup passes. Public authorization/RLS, production dispatch, worker authentication, aggregate/fleet quotas, provider execution and GA remain pending. See [the admission contract](docs/hosted-build-admission.md).",
work-graph.json:14107:      "buildCoordinatorCheckpoint": "The internal build coordinator now consumes durable Oban intents, commits start before dispatch, reconciles stable worker operations across lease transfers, and retains capacity through uncertain cancellation or timeout. Guarded release/retry and lease yielding pass root and independent review: 261 host tests, including 19 producer controls, 14 independent controls and one actual asynchronous Oban processor check. Two identity tests requiring isolated Linux networking remain skipped. All 92 current/archived inputs and 21 command logs verify; production fixtures are absent and owned Oban/PostgreSQL/scratch cleanup passes. The provider remains modeled and unconfigured; public authorization, worker authentication/isolation, fleet quotas, signing, cloud operations and GA remain pending. See [the coordinator checkpoint](docs/hosted-build-coordinator-checkpoint.md).",
work-graph.json:14114:      "workerControllerImplementationCheckpoint": "The first per-operation Worker/SQLite controller is implemented but independent review rejects it: 28 producer groups pass; five of eight new groups pass and three fail. Final claims can survive a newer authority watermark, and accepted effect/claim clock samples are not persisted. Root verifies the producer source/archive, installed dependencies and outputs plus 48 review artifacts and 12 archived fixtures. All 58 locked development dependencies are recorded. A separate V2 repair is assigned; no production provider or controller is enabled. See docs/hosted-worker-controller-checkpoint.md.",
work-graph.json:14118:      "workerControllerLinuxAcceptanceCheckpoint": "The controller restart repair now passes Linux CI at `7744c1cc`: 20 process-identity controls and all 71 existing controller groups pass, including eight actual workerd SIGKILL recoveries. Root verifies 27 source files against the commit, six command/output/cleanup records, 153 removed persistent fixtures and nine unchanged compiled production closure files. The earlier Linux failure is preserved. Pending-operation registry, deployed recovery/time/provider/restore, signing and GA remain open. See docs/hosted-worker-controller-linux-ci-checkpoint.md.",
work-graph.json:14122:      "pendingRegistryComponentsIntegration": "The corrected pending registry/audit components are integrated, with exact reviewed source and nine matching compiled outputs. Root passes the live 71-group controller suite plus 20 process-identity controls; all six commands and owned fixture cleanup pass. The derivative eight schema/four terminal controls and five independent controls remain scoped component evidence. Engine integration is withheld for two independently reproduced provider-identity/post-verifier-fence defects under repair; operation and scheduled/public wiring remain pending. See docs/hosted-worker-pending-registry-components-integration.md.",
work-graph.json:14124:      "pendingRegistryComponentLinux CI": "Registry component checkpoint 4a4d8b73 passes Linux Worker controller CI. Root verifies all 32 archived source files against the pushed commit, 71 controller groups, 20 process-identity controls, eight actual SIGKILL recoveries, six complete command groups and 153 removed storage fixtures. The deployed entry remains unchanged; component integration does not qualify real providers, clock, restore or GA. See verification/github-ci-4a4d8b73-controller/artifact-review.json.",
