s releasechecks and allSwift/VM/Goengine jobs. Atomicpreflight review identifies mandatory corrections; the original configuredstartup review required endpointLF fix, now resolved in the separately accepted startup slice. No product/GA acceptance. Configured startup now integrated after independent31focused cases and corrected95Linux passes; root93host passes/2explicitLinux-only skips plus release and cleanup checks. NoHTTP/currentDB/provider/cloud/native orGA acceptance. Checkpoint4250e05a LinuxhostedCI passes93tests/2explicitnamespace skips,release and cleanup;62archiveinputs matchcommit. Both preceding e58e84ca and current4250e05a pass all three engine jobs. No gate status change.",
gates/ga.json:356:      "exactReactorDiagnosticCheckpoint": "The exact 53,777,114-byte full Swift FieldLog reactor passes owned validation of 79,832 bodies and 6,505,659 instructions, adoption and runtime construction. Initialization stops at a test-only 64-entry release observer assertion; neither corpus call runs. Root verifies 246 sealed files plus three external bindings. The original failure is preserved, the process group is empty and owned scratch is removed. A narrow test-only observer repair is underway; full-reactor execution, native/public/signed use and GA remain pending. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-diagnostic.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
gates/ga.json:358:      "exactReactorAfterObserverCheckpoint": "The full Swift FieldLog reactor now passes complete owned validation and real initialization. Its first corpus stops at the unchanged CacheWork limit: attempted 64,000,001 of 64,000,000, after 24,054 decodes and 23,990 evictions; the second corpus is unrun. Original consuming cleanup returns primary reservations, tickets and live counters to zero while retaining the failure. Root verifies 214 sealed members and four external bindings; owned scratch is removed. Cache-work optimization analysis is underway without widening bounds. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
gates/ga.json:359:      "cacheResetElisionSelection": "Root selects a narrow private Swift cache candidate after source-bound diagnosis: two redundant 512-slot clearing loops account for at least 24,631,296 credits in the failed target run. A finite actual-cache fixture confirms the cost; this is not measured target CPU attribution or a completion prediction. The additive contract removes only those operations, retaining initialized scratch, explicit pass-boundary checks and all original limits. Implementation and acceptance are pending; no new full-reactor attempt is selected. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-contract.md and verification/swift-cache-reset-elision-root-selection/selection.json.",
gates/ga.json:360:      "cacheResetElisionCheckpoint": "Root accepts and integrates the private Swift cache reset elimination: two redundant 512-slot writes are removed, retaining initialized scratch and pass-boundary checks under unchanged limits. The producer matrix passes default/compatibility/all-feature Debug and Release with existing ignores retained; six fresh root live tests pass at VM closure b28da766c84b6353a4511e2fc3fbcb0d4302d5b8a5a74da1ee3d7fb776ca2c11. Owned build targets are removed. A separate unchanged full-reactor attempt is being prepared; no target, native, signed, published FieldLog or GA pass is claimed. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-checkpoint.md.",
gates/ga.json:364:      "residentIndexCandidateCheckpoint": "The isolated private Swift resident index passes 626 all-feature Release tests with nine inherited ignores, 29 cache Debug tests, default/compatibility suites, Clippy and scoped formatting. Root verifies all 570 sealed members and the unchanged live VM closure. The finite 256-hit fixture uses 2,048 versus 8,832 credits; fixed cache accounting increases by 840 bytes and foundation accounting by 384 bytes under unchanged limits. Independent review is underway; no live integration or full-reactor retry is selected. See docs/swift-cache-resident-index.md.",
gates/ga.json:368:      "currentCheckpoint": "Underlying fixture-only envelope source and bounded accounting have scoped independent host acceptance: 78 producer methods, 14 exact-source independent methods plus 2 separate test-overlay methods, API1+8, 21,714 fresh candidate comparisons and 32 layouts; root verified 407 source/accounting/review members. No semantic replay, live VM/CLI/target or GA acceptance. Portable CI runner round1 was rejected for ambiguous compiler identity and unrelated diagnostic spans. Corrected runner passes 32 normal/optimized controls and one fresh full Rust1.99 host closure; independent correction review now passes and root accepts the scoped runner. Exact CI wiring is applied; delivery and actual Rust1.98.1 CI remain pending. The earlier complete target still fails Corpus1 CacheWork; no optimization has been accepted from this fixture work.",
gates/ga.json:370:      "decodePlanReuseAccountingReview": "Root accepts the finite decode-plan source/accounting review after verifying 620 sealed files, five external bindings and 4,752 command/source bindings. Thirty-five of 36 named executions pass; the sole original exact-phase fixture failure is preserved and its measured correction passes. No production defect was found; original limits remain unchanged. Isolated full host regressions and measured fixture updates are selected under docs/swift-decode-plan-regression-contract.md. Live integration and another full-reactor attempt remain unselected. See docs/swift-decode-plan-reuse-accounting-review.md and verification/swift-decode-plan-reuse-diagnosis-root-review/accounting-review-acceptance.json.",
