gates/ga.json:12497:      "currentCheckpoint": "The contextual cleanup diagnostic repair is independently reviewed, root accepted and integrated without normalization at 128-file source closure 1e89853d56f0ae46720cb0e9d72a4a2a13003f777e1d01f65db154f30782ed9c. Root verifies 2,010 upstream bindings and 31 integration files; fresh 282 all-feature Release library tests, sixteen Frozen Release tests, Swift Clippy and whitespace checks pass. Active live-count failures now retain the current instruction/resource/count; legacy cleanup remains cursorless and the first failure remains immutable. Owned command groups and 166,955,154 bytes of scratch are cleaned. Defined/indirect calls and the full dispatcher contract are next. Original-source diagnostics, Ready/public invocation, native/FieldLog/physical and G08/GA remain pending. See `docs/swift-cleanup-diagnostic-integration-checkpoint.md`. Pushed diagnostic checkpoint 2fb0db99 passes all three terminal engine jobs and 38 steps, with none skipped. Root selects the coherent defined/indirect calls plus complete private dispatcher contract after 139 bindings, eight fresh compiler contexts and four expected borrow rejections. CD01-CD24 runtime and complete positive accounting remain pending; the uncalled compiler witness is not execution or reservation evidence. See `docs/swift-calls-dispatch-contract.md` and `verification/swift-calls-dispatch-root-review/selection.json`.",
gates/ga.json:12498:      "lifecycleTestCheckpoint": "The private lifecycle test suite is now expanded from 23 to 49 identities and integrated without changing production engine bytes. All four Swift/all Debug/Release contexts pass (196 executions), six compiler-negative checks pass, and independent review passes 49 tests plus two controls over eight variants. Root verifies both packets and passes a fresh 49-test live replay at exact 132-file closure `64a3d9c52ade75ec16de10191f14257fb75ff358c366666cf47809e2b9a7f0de`. All owned build targets are removed. Every SL01-SL23 row remains partial; table mutation, the full reactor, public/signed/native entry, FieldLog and GA remain pending. See docs/swift-reactor-lifecycle-remaining-checkpoint.md.",
gates/ga.json:12499:      "latestLifecycleCI": "Checkpoint `50f70a79` passes the complete Engine CI after the test-only deadline fixture repair: all three jobs and all 38 steps succeed, with none skipped. The Linux VM job passes 391 all-feature tests and 361 Swift-only tests in both Debug and Release; Swift, services and separate Phoenix CI also pass. The earlier `ccd8e4c3` three-test Linux setup failure remains preserved. See `verification/github-ci-50f70a79-engine/receipt.json`, `verification/github-ci-50f70a79-vm/receipt.json` and `verification/github-ci-50f70a79-phoenix/receipt.json`.",
gates/ga.json:12500:      "exactReactorDiagnosticCheckpoint": "The exact 53,777,114-byte full Swift FieldLog reactor passes owned validation of 79,832 bodies and 6,505,659 instructions, adoption and runtime construction. Initialization stops at a test-only 64-entry release observer assertion; neither corpus call runs. Root verifies 246 sealed files plus three external bindings. The original failure is preserved, the process group is empty and owned scratch is removed. A narrow test-only observer repair is underway; full-reactor execution, native/public/signed use and GA remain pending. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-diagnostic.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
gates/ga.json:12502:      "exactReactorAfterObserverCheckpoint": "The full Swift FieldLog reactor now passes complete owned validation and real initialization. Its first corpus stops at the unchanged CacheWork limit: attempted 64,000,001 of 64,000,000, after 24,054 decodes and 23,990 evictions; the second corpus is unrun. Original consuming cleanup returns primary reservations, tickets and live counters to zero while retaining the failure. Root verifies 214 sealed members and four external bindings; owned scratch is removed. Cache-work optimization analysis is underway without widening bounds. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
gates/ga.json:12503:      "cacheResetElisionSelection": "Root selects a narrow private Swift cache candidate after source-bound diagnosis: two redundant 512-slot clearing loops account for at least 24,631,296 credits in the failed target run. A finite actual-cache fixture confirms the cost; this is not measured target CPU attribution or a completion prediction. The additive contract removes only those operations, retaining initialized scratch, explicit pass-boundary checks and all original limits. Implementation and acceptance are pending; no new full-reactor attempt is selected. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-contract.md and verification/swift-cache-reset-elision-root-selection/selection.json.",
gates/ga.json:12504:      "cacheResetElisionCheckpoint": "Root accepts and integrates the private Swift cache reset elimination: two redundant 512-slot writes are removed, retaining initialized scratch and pass-boundary checks under unchanged limits. The producer matrix passes default/compatibility/all-feature Debug and Release with existing ignores retained; six fresh root live tests pass at VM closure b28da766c84b6353a4511e2fc3fbcb0d4302d5b8a5a74da1ee3d7fb776ca2c11. Owned build targets are removed. A separate unchanged full-reactor attempt is being prepared; no target, native, signed, published FieldLog or GA pass is claimed. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-checkpoint.md.",
