mixer-product-plan.md:392:Resource enforcement is mandatory; initial experimental numeric ceilings are revisable under Section 20.3. The coordinator may select bounded, nondefault host experiments within existing authorization without a new user approval for each variant. Preserve the failed baseline, account for changed storage/work structures and retain all active holds. Such selection does not alter public/installed production policy.
mixer-product-plan.md:677:Test large text, VoiceOver/TalkBack, right-to-left layout, multiple locales, dark mode, reduced motion, keyboard input, rotation, process death, denied permissions, constrained network, low disk, and low-memory behavior. Physical device tests are required for latency, memory, energy, camera, push, purchases, and lifecycle claims.
mixer-product-plan.md:725:### 20.3 Calibrate experimental limits against real workloads
mixer-product-plan.md:920:### 24.4 Aggressive blocker experiments and integration priority
mixer-product-plan.md:946:Every delegated task explicitly selects its role's model and `reasoning_effort: "xhigh"`; do not rely on inherited models or default effort. Ordinary tasks use `gpt-6.1-sol`; Section 24.4 escalation tasks use `gpt-6-astra`. Use `fork_turns: "none"` and include the complete bounded task contract, relevant file paths, decisions, interfaces, known failed hypotheses and verification requirements. Record the actual model and reasoning level with each task's completion evidence. Use Astra escalation proactively when the trigger is met; do not wait for another user request to try a stronger agent.
mixer-product-plan.md:987:- The coordinator decomposes ready packages into implementation, test, review and dogfood tasks, using Sol 6.1 Extra High ordinarily and Astra 6 Extra High for Section 24.4 escalation. Prioritize completed vertical slices and discriminating experiments over additional disconnected preparation.
mixer-product-plan.md:1039:| Shorebird | Patches Flutter/Dart; native changes still require the relevant native release path. | Strong adjacent competition, but does not deliver the requested Swift authoring model. [Shorebird FAQ](https://docs.shorebird.dev/code-push/faq/) |
mixer-product-plan.md:1246:| Blocker escalation: Astra 6 Extra High | Selected under October 28 user instruction | Explicit `gpt-6-astra` with `xhigh` and fresh context for competing experiments, architecture challenge and difficult review under Section 24.4. |
mixer-product-plan.md:1247:| Experimental resource ceilings | Empirical hypotheses under Sections 20.3/24.4 | Preserve failed baselines and enforce finite safeguards; compare candidate profiles before selecting measured production budgets. |
mixer-product-plan.md:1305:  - notifications.push
mixer-product-plan.md:1376:| [Shorebird FAQ](https://docs.shorebird.dev/code-push/faq/) | Flutter/Dart adjacent product and native-change boundary. |
mixer-product-plan.md:1391:Commit coherent, validated implementation and evidence slices as work progresses, and periodically push meaningful checkpoints to the user-owned [snowdamiz/mixer repository](https://github.com/snowdamiz/mixer). The root integrator coordinates pushes to `main`, preserves unfinished agent work, avoids force-pushing, and inspects hosted CI after each push. This source-delivery authorization does not authorize production deployments, store submissions, or customer messages. `PLAN.md` records the delivery workflow and current execution constraints.
mixer-product-plan.md:1397:The immediate execution priority is working integrated FieldLog behavior through the public shared Swift SDK, with native iOS/Android work and bounded VM blocker experiments advancing in parallel where dependencies permit. Existing implementation and receipts retain their actual scope. Run the Section 24.4 escalation process when progress stalls; historical per-run freezes preserve old evidence and do not permanently prohibit a newly selected experiment. Current explicit user pauses, process/custody restrictions, automated security denials and release authority still apply. The completion target remains the full independently owned commercial product described above.


